hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21467","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Yahya ibn Yamar from Sulayman ibn Surad from Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, who said: I recited a verse, and Ibn Masud recited contrary to it, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Did you not teach me such and such a verse. He said: Yes. So Ibn Masud said: Did you not teach it to me as such and such. So he said: Yes, both of you are good, correct. He said: So I said to him, and he struck my chest and said: O Ubayy ibn Kab, I was taught the Quran and it was said to me: Upon one harf or upon two ahruf. He said: So the angel with me said: Upon two ahruf. So I said: Upon two ahruf. So he said: Upon two ahruf or three. So the angel with me said: Upon three. So I said: Upon three, until it reached seven ahruf, none of them except healing, sufficient: If you say Forgiving, Merciful, or you say Hearing, Knowing, or Knowing, Hearing, so Allah is thus, so long as you do not seal a verse of torment with mercy or a verse of mercy with torment."
"21468","Bahz narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Yamar from Sulayman ibn Surad al-Khuzai from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I recited a verse, and Ibn Masud recited contrary to it, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"21469","Abdullah narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid al-Qaysi narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Yamar from Sulayman ibn Surad from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I recited a verse, and Ibn Masud recited contrary to it, and another man recited contrary to it, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"21470","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Suqayr al-Abdi from Sulayman ibn Surad from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I heard a man reciting, so I said: Who taught you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: Go to him. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Question this one. So he said: Recite. So he recited, and he said: You did well. So I said to him: Did you not teach me such and such. He said: Yes, and you did well. So I said with my hands: You did well twice. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand upon my chest, then said: O Allah, remove doubt from Ubayy. So I poured sweat and my belly filled with awe. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ubayy, two angels came to me, so one said: Recite upon one harf, and the other said: Increase him. So I said: Increase me. He said: Recite upon two ahruf. And the other said: Increase him. So I said: Increase me. So he said: Recite upon three. And the other said: Increase him. So I said: Increase me. He said: Recite upon four ahruf. The other said: Increase him. I said: Increase me. He said: Recite upon five ahruf. The other said: Increase him. I said: Increase me. He said: Recite upon six. The other said: Increase him. He said: Recite upon seven ahruf, so the Quran was sent down upon seven ahruf."
"21471","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warakani narrated to us: Sharik informed us from Abu Ishaq from Sulayman from Ubayy ibn Kab, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two angels came to me, so one said to the other: Teach him. He said: Upon how many. He said: A harf. He said: Increase him. He said: Until it reached seven ahruf."
